---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalShell from '../components/legal/LegalShell.astro';
import { legalPage } from '../data/legal';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const page = legalPage(
  'privacy-policy',
  '/privacy-policy/',
  'Privacy Policy | Tip Top Hybrid',
  'How Tip Top Hybrid collects, uses and protects the information you send through our website, estimate forms and phone calls.',
);
---

<BaseLayout page={page}>
  <LegalShell title="Privacy Policy" updated="November 15, 2026">
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Tip Top Hybrid</strong> (“we”, “us”, “our”) handles
      information collected through <strong>www.tiptophybrid.com</strong> (the “Site”), our online
      estimate and contact forms, and calls or texts to our shop. By using the Site or sending us a
      request, you agree to this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you submit an estimate or contact form, call us, text us or email us, we may collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name, email address and phone number;</li>
      <li>Vehicle details such as year, make, model and the symptoms or service you describe;</li>
      <li>Any other information you choose to include in a message.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like most websites, our Site and the
      analytics and advertising tools listed below may record your IP address, approximate location,
      device and browser type, referring page, pages viewed, and how you interact with the Site.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Calls.</strong> Calls to the numbers published on this Site may be routed through a
      call-tracking service and may be recorded or logged for quality, training and record-keeping.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not ask for payment card details, Social Security numbers or other sensitive information
      through this Site, and you should not send them through a form.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Respond to your request, prepare estimates and schedule service;</li>
      <li>Contact you by phone, text or email about your request and your vehicle;</li>
      <li>Keep records of the work we quote, perform and warrant;</li>
      <li>Improve the Site, our services and our advertising (for example, measuring which pages and ads generate enquiries);</li>
      <li>Protect against fraud, abuse and security issues; and</li>
      <li>Comply with legal, tax and record-keeping obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Cookies and tracking technologies</h2>
    <p>
      The Site uses cookies, pixels and similar technologies. The main third-party tools we use are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics 4 and Google Ads</strong> — traffic measurement, conversion tracking and remarketing;</li>
      <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> — aggregated session analytics such as heatmaps and click maps; and</li>
      <li><strong>Call-tracking scripts</strong> — to attribute calls to the page or ad that generated them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, although parts of the Site may then
      work differently. You can also opt out of personalised advertising through
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>,
      the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>,
      <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">NAI opt-out</a>, or
      <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">DAA opt-out</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Who we share information with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only as needed to run our business:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Service providers</strong> that host the Site, deliver our forms and email, provide analytics and advertising, and route phone calls;</li>
      <li><strong>Our staff and technicians</strong> who handle your enquiry or repair;</li>
      <li><strong>Professional advisers, insurers or authorities</strong> where required by law or necessary to protect our rights or safety; and</li>
      <li><strong>A successor business</strong> if our business is sold or merged.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Calls, texts and your consent</h2>
    <p>
      By submitting a form or otherwise giving us your phone number, you consent to be contacted by
      phone, text message or email at that number about your enquiry, including by automated means
      where permitted by law. Message and data rates may apply. Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to opt out
      of texts or <strong>HELP</strong> for help. Consent is not a condition of receiving an estimate
      or service, and you can ask us to stop contacting you at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>6. How long we keep information</h2>
    <p>
      We keep enquiry and repair records for as long as needed for the purposes described above,
      including warranty, accounting and legal requirements, and then delete or anonymise them.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards to protect the information we hold.
      No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute
      security.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your California privacy rights</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act (as amended by the CPRA)
      gives you the right to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Know what personal information we collect, use and disclose;</li>
      <li>Request a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
      <li>Ask us to delete or correct your personal information;</li>
      <li>Opt out of the “sale” or “sharing” of personal information — we do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising beyond the analytics and advertising tools described above, which you can limit using the opt-outs in section 3; and</li>
      <li>Not be discriminated against for exercising these rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To make a request, call us on <strong>{SITE.phone}</strong> or email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> with “Privacy request” in the subject line. We
      may ask for information to verify your identity before acting. An authorised agent may submit a
      request on your behalf with written permission.
    </p>
    <p>
      California’s “Shine the Light” law (Civil Code §1798.83) also lets California residents ask
      about personal information disclosed to third parties for their direct marketing — we do not
      disclose personal information for third-party direct marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children
      under 13. If you believe a child has submitted information, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Other websites</h2>
    <p>
      The Site links to third-party sites such as Google Maps and social media. Their privacy
      practices are governed by their own policies, which we recommend reading.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The revision date above shows when it last changed,
      and the current version always applies to information collected after it is posted.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Tip Top Hybrid<br />
      {SITE.street}, Upland, CA 91786<br />
      Phone: <strong>{SITE.phone}</strong><br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
    </p>
  </LegalShell>
</BaseLayout>
